      "content": "To check for vertical instability, visually inspect each interlock point and feel for any tilting or play before tightening the braces. A good rule of thumb is to lightly tap the loaded pallet close to a support beam; if it doesn't continue to rattle or feel solid, the stack is likely unbalanced and risks tipping forward. You can also use a spirit level or ask your laser level customers to verify that the top of the pallet doesn't settle unevenly over time.",
